# L §4.2 (round 12) calendar(weekends [...]) lists "the weekdays that are never business days (mon tue wed thu fri
# sat sun, ISO 8601's days 1 to 7 ...)". A Friday-Saturday weekend: 2026-03-05 is a Thursday, 2026-03-06 a Friday,
# 2026-03-08 a Sunday (`weekday`, L §4.2: 1 for Monday to 7 for Sunday); add_business(d, 1, cal) is the first business
# day after d.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [fri, sat])

ask q1: weekday(2026-03-06), is_business(2026-03-06, len), is_business(2026-03-08, len)
ask q2: add_business(2026-03-05, 1, len)
=== expect
q1: (5, false, true)
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 2026-03-08
  cut 2026-12-31
